---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CommunityClip from '../../components/CommunityClip.astro';
import { installVideoGallery } from '../../data/communityClips';
import { SITE } from '../../lib/site';
const lang = 'en' as const;
const videoGallery = installVideoGallery(lang);
const toc = [
  { id: 'install-demo', label: 'Codex walkthrough' },
  { id: 'requirements', label: 'Requirements' },
  { id: 'connect', label: 'Connect agent' },
  { id: 'cli', label: 'Optional CLI' },
  { id: 'ghidra', label: 'Ghidra (BYO)' },
  { id: 'first', label: 'First question' },
  { id: 'see-others', label: 'See how others use it' },
  { id: 'related-videos', label: 'Related videos' },
  { id: 'actions-demo', label: 'Actions demo' },
  { id: 'codespaces', label: 'Codespaces lab' },
  { id: 'related', label: 'Related guides' },
  { id: 'links', label: 'Upstream links' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  lang={lang}
  title="Install REA (rea-agents) — community guide | rea.run"
  description="Install REA with npx rea-agents setup, MCP registration, and bring-your-own Ghidra. Community paraphrase of upstream; verify on GitHub."
  path="/docs/install/"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12">
    <div class="docs-layout">
      <aside class="docs-toc hidden md:block">
        <p class="section-kicker mb-3">On this page</p>
        {toc.map((item) => <a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a>)}
      </aside>

      <article class="prose-page">
        <p class="badge">Docs · Install</p>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-4xl">Install REA</h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-[var(--color-muted)]">
          Community paraphrase of upstream install notes. Product behavior is defined by
          <a href={SITE.upstreamRepo}>github.com/morluto/rea</a>
          and the <code>rea-agents</code> package on npm. Versions change — re-check before you automate.
        </p>

        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">Use on software you are authorized to analyze. <a class="quiet-link" href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></p>

        <h2 id="install-demo">Codex walkthrough</h2>
        <p>
          Want the whole loop in one sitting? The install demo pins <code>rea-agents@6.4.0</code>, checks Node, registers Codex, opens Chrome on port 9222, and has Codex recover the public dinosaur game’s acceleration rule — then build a one-file game with a speed slider.
        </p>
        <p><a class="btn" href="/docs/install-demo/">Open the Codex install demo</a></p>

        <h2 id="requirements">Requirements</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div class="step-card"><span class="step-num">1</span><div><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Node</strong><p class="mt-1 !text-sm">22 (22.19+), 24 (24.11+), or 26+ plus npm (per upstream).</p></div></div>
          <div class="step-card"><span class="step-num">2</span><div><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">MCP client</strong><p class="mt-1 !text-sm">Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Windsurf, Grok Build, or other MCP clients — or CLI alone.</p></div></div>
          <div class="step-card"><span class="step-num">3</span><div><strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Native engines</strong><p class="mt-1 !text-sm">Deep native analysis needs existing Hopper, Ghidra, or IDA. Static JS/Electron does not.</p></div></div>
        </div>

        <h2 id="connect">Connect your coding agent</h2>
        <p>Ask your agent to run setup with approval, or run it yourself:</p>
        <pre><code>npx rea-agents@latest setup</code></pre>
        <p>
          Choose your client, review the plan, and approve changes. Setup registers the MCP server and matching investigation skill, backing up existing config. <strong>Restart the client</strong> afterward.
        </p>
        <p>Manual MCP registration shape (confirm against upstream if your client needs hand-edited JSON):</p>
        <pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "rea": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "rea-agents@latest", "mcp"]
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>
        <p>Pin an exact <code>rea-agents@VERSION</code> when you need reproducible installs.</p>

        <h2 id="cli">Optional: global CLI</h2>
        <pre><code>npm install --global rea-agents</code></pre>

        <h2 id="ghidra">Ghidra (bring your own)</h2>
        <p>REA does not install Ghidra or Java. Export absolute paths, then doctor + setup:</p>
        <pre><code>{`export GHIDRA_INSTALL_DIR=/absolute/path/to/ghidra_PUBLIC
export JAVA_HOME=/absolute/path/to/jdk-21
npx -y rea-agents@latest doctor --provider ghidra --json
npx rea-agents@latest setup`}</code></pre>
        <p>
          Supported host / Ghidra / JDK combinations are defined upstream — see
          <a href="https://github.com/morluto/rea/blob/main/docs/installation.md">docs/installation.md</a> in the GitHub repo.
        </p>

        <h2 id="first">First question to try</h2>
        <p>After reconnecting the agent, give an <strong>absolute path</strong> to a target you may analyze and a specific question (entry points, export paths, a named feature). Prefer Evidence + unknowns over speculative narratives.</p>




        <h2 id="see-others">See how others use it</h2>
        <p>After install, start with three community demos on devices the authors own (hosted here, not hotlinked from X): a status-bar toilet remote, an own TV, and an own body-composition scale.</p>
        <div id="related-videos">
          {videoGallery.map((clip) => (
            <CommunityClip
              lang="en"
              src={clip.src}
              poster={clip.poster}
              frame={clip.frame}
              kicker={clip.kicker}
              title={clip.title}
              blurb={clip.blurb}
              href={clip.href}
              hrefLabel={clip.hrefLabel}
              attribution={clip.attribution}
              note={clip.note}
            />
          ))}
        </div>

        <h2 id="actions-demo">GitHub Actions demo (no local install)</h2>
        <p>
          Prefer a pipeline over installing locally? Open
          <a href="https://github.com/ylwl1997/rea-run-lab">ylwl1997/rea-run-lab</a>
          → <strong>Actions</strong> → workflow <strong>demo-smoke</strong> → <strong>Run workflow</strong>
          (branch <code>main</code>). When the run finishes, open the run summary → <strong>Artifacts</strong> → download
          <code>smoke-report</code> (JSON + HTML Evidence-style teaching report).
        </p>
        <div class="try-tracks" aria-label="Lab try tracks">
          <a class="try-track" href="https://github.com/ylwl1997/rea-run-lab/actions/workflows/demo-smoke.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span class="try-track-kicker">GitHub Actions</span>
            <span class="try-track-title">Open Actions demo</span>
            <span class="try-track-blurb">demo-smoke · Run workflow · Artifacts</span>
          </a>
          <a class="try-track" href="https://codespaces.new/ylwl1997/rea-run-lab?quickstart=1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span class="try-track-kicker">Codespaces</span>
            <span class="try-track-title">用 Codespaces 试跑 / Open lab</span>
            <span class="try-track-blurb">Node 22 · bundled demo only</span>
          </a>
        </div>
        <ul>
          <li>Primary path: download <strong>Artifacts</strong> (<code>smoke-report</code>). Latest report may also appear on the lab’s GitHub Pages when the pages job succeeds.</li>
          <li>Runs only the <strong>bundled self-owned</strong> Electron-shaped demo under <code>demo/</code> — no arbitrary binary uploads.</li>
          <li>Authorized / own targets only; see <a href="/faq/legal-boundary/">legal boundary</a>.</li>
          <li>Deeper Electron Evidence teaching: <a href="/showcase/rea-playbook/">rea-playbook</a>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="codespaces">Try in GitHub Codespaces</h2>
        <p>
          Prefer a disposable cloud shell? Open the public lab
          <a href="https://github.com/ylwl1997/rea-run-lab">ylwl1997/rea-run-lab</a>
          in Codespaces (Node 22 Dev Container), then run
          <code>npx rea-agents@latest setup</code> against the <strong>bundled self-owned Electron-shaped demo</strong> only.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">Same lab as the Actions track above — interactive shell when you want it.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>No arbitrary binary uploads — lab ships one teaching target under <code>demo/</code>.</li>
          <li>Authorized / own targets only; see <a href="/faq/legal-boundary/">legal boundary</a>.</li>
          <li>Same lab repo as the Actions demo — two tracks, one <code>demo/</code>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="related">Related guides</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/showcase/thinkszyg-toilet-ble/">Case: status-bar toilet remote</a></li>
          <li><a href="/showcase/greco-dev-tv/">Case: greco’s own TV</a></li>
          <li><a href="/showcase/brorlandi-miscale/">Case: BrOrlandi’s own scale</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/install-demo/">Codex install demo — dinosaur speed rule</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/mcp-clients/">MCP client install matrix &amp; skill paths</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/android-adb/">Android ADB device lane (6.4+)</a></li>
          <li><a href="/faq/setup-vs-providers/">Does setup install Ghidra/Hopper/IDA?</a></li>
          <li><a href="/faq/macos-ghidra-decompiler/">macOS Ghidra decompiler missing</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/rea-agents-6-4-0/">REA 6.4.0 operator guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/windows-ghidra/">Windows × Ghidra wiring</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/ghidra-large-binaries/">Large binaries &amp; Ghidra startup deadlines</a></li>
          <li><a href="/docs/linux-fedora/">Linux / Fedora install notes</a></li>
          <li><a href="/faq/tmpdir-dot-path/">TMPDIR / hidden-directory pitfalls</a></li>
          <li><a href="/faq/">FAQ hub</a></li>
        </ul>
        <h2 id="links">Upstream links</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={SITE.upstreamRepo}>GitHub: morluto/rea</a></li>
          <li><a href={SITE.upstreamNpm}>npm: rea-agents</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/ghidra-mcp-with-rea/">Community: Ghidra MCP with REA</a></li>
          <li><a href="/compliance/">Compliance</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
